222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 100 0 R
/T (In Somalia specifically, the scale of exclusion is severe as nomadic pastoralists constitute roughly two-thirds of the population, yet only around 22 percent of pastoralist children access formal education, a gap compounded by the practice of female genital mutilation, which affects an estimated 98 percent of Somali girls and is frequently followed by school withdrawal due to resulting health complications and early child marriage \(Jama & Barre, 2019\). This is corroborated by UNICEF's regional reporting, which found that the number of children at risk of dropping out of school across Ethiopia, Kenya and Somalia tripled within three months during a recent drought period; from 1.1 million to an estimated 3.3 million, placing adolescent girls at substantially elevated risk of early marriage as a negative household coping mechanism \(Wakhisi et al, 2025; UNICEF USA, 2024\). )
/E (In Somalia specifically, the scale of exclusion is severe as nomadic pastoralists constitute roughly two-thirds of the population, yet only around 22 percent of pastoralist children access formal education, a gap compounded by the practice of female genital mutilation, which affects an estimated 98 percent of Somali girls and is frequently followed by school withdrawal due to resulting health complications and early child marriage \(Jama & Barre, 2019\). This is corroborated by UNICEF's regional reporting, which found that the number of children at risk of dropping out of school across Ethiopia, Kenya and Somalia tripled within three months during a recent drought period; from 1.1 million to an estimated 3.3 million, placing adolescent girls at substantially elevated risk of early marriage as a negative household coping mechanism \(Wakhisi et al, 2025; UNICEF USA, 2024\). )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 100 0 R
/T (Evidence on effective interventions is more encouraging. A longitudinal study of AMREF Health Africa's Community-Led Alternative Rite of Passage \(CL-ARP\) programme in Kajiado County, Kenya, designed to prevent female genital mutilation/cutting and child marriage while keeping girls in school, followed 2,647 girls over three years and found that 98 percent remained free of FGM/C, 99 percent avoided child, early or forced marriage, and 98 percent remained enrolled in school, although girls who experienced threats or violence remained more likely to experience all three negative outcomes despite programme participation \(Kawai et al., 2025\). This finding is directly relevant to this brief's recommendations, that culturally grounded, community-led alternatives to harmful practices can produce durable educational gains when they address the social drivers of dropout directly, rather than focusing on school access alone.)
/E (Evidence on effective interventions is more encouraging. A longitudinal study of AMREF Health Africa's Community-Led Alternative Rite of Passage \(CL-ARP\) programme in Kajiado County, Kenya, designed to prevent female genital mutilation/cutting and child marriage while keeping girls in school, followed 2,647 girls over three years and found that 98 percent remained free of FGM/C, 99 percent avoided child, early or forced marriage, and 98 percent remained enrolled in school, although girls who experienced threats or violence remained more likely to experience all three negative outcomes despite programme participation \(Kawai et al., 2025\). This finding is directly relevant to this brief's recommendations, that culturally grounded, community-led alternatives to harmful practices can produce durable educational gains when they address the social drivers of dropout directly, rather than focusing on school access alone.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 100 0 R
/T (Finally, a broader review of evolving global approaches to educating nomadic children cautions that policy attention has often overemphasized physical access logistics,  getting a school building or mobile unit near enough to reach, albeit at the expense of considering whether the content and structure of learning itself fits nomadic livelihoods and cultural values, a critique that applies directly to this study's parallel finding that indigenous ecological knowledge remains excluded from formal curricula even where physical access to schooling improves \(Dyer, 2016\). )
/E (Finally, a broader review of evolving global approaches to educating nomadic children cautions that policy attention has often overemphasized physical access logistics,  getting a school building or mobile unit near enough to reach, albeit at the expense of considering whether the content and structure of learning itself fits nomadic livelihoods and cultural values, a critique that applies directly to this study's parallel finding that indigenous ecological knowledge remains excluded from formal curricula even where physical access to schooling improves \(Dyer, 2016\). )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
