/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 101 0 R
/T (Respondents consistently described formal education as insufficiently adapted to nomadic and semi-nomadic communities. Fixed school locations, long travel distances, insecurity, rigid academic calendars, seasonal migration and household labour demands combine to produce low enrolment and dropout, with girls affected disproportionately. This finding was reported by key informants across all four study countries i.e.  Kenya, Somalia, Tanzania and South Africa, thus indicating a shared structural gap rather than an isolated national issue.)
/E (Respondents consistently described formal education as insufficiently adapted to nomadic and semi-nomadic communities. Fixed school locations, long travel distances, insecurity, rigid academic calendars, seasonal migration and household labour demands combine to produce low enrolment and dropout, with girls affected disproportionately. This finding was reported by key informants across all four study countries i.e.  Kenya, Somalia, Tanzania and South Africa, thus indicating a shared structural gap rather than an isolated national issue.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
