<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 106 0 R
/E (Prioritize Somalia's severe exclusion gap specifically - target investment toward closing the gap between Somalia's roughly two-thirds pastoralist population share and the estimated one-fifth of pastoralist children currently accessing formal education, recognizing this as a distinct, higher-severity case within the East & Horn of Africa \(EHoA\) region.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 106 0 R
/T (3. Linking Drought Response and Education Continuity)
/E (3. Linking Drought Response and Education Continuity)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 601 0 R
/E (Build education continuity safeguards directly into drought and humanitarian response planning - treat school dropout and early marriage as predictable, trackable drought impacts and not secondary consequences especially against documented evidence that at-risk-of-dropout children across Ethiopia, Kenya and Somalia tripled within three months during a recent drought period for example.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 602 0 R
/E (Connect education continuity planning to anticipatory action systems - integrate education-continuity triggers into emerging anticipatory-action frameworks such as IGAD's Forecasts to Local Action \(FOLA\) approach, so that education risk is monitored and acted on using the same forecast-based triggers already being developed for livelihood protection \(CLARE Programme, 2026\))
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 106 0 R
/T (4. Integrating Indigenous Knowledge into Curricula)
/E (4. Integrating Indigenous Knowledge into Curricula)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 603 0 R
/E (Co-design curriculum content with women knowledge-holders - ensure formal education validates and builds on pastoral ecological knowledge e.g. weather patterns, livestock management, seed preservation rather than just treating it as separate from or inferior to standard curricula. Recognize that there is no single way of learning and that there are many ways of knowing. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
